searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"MedAdapters","doc":"Opt-in behaviour-driven signal compute and external media adapter layer for\nMedEx (`MedAdapters.Inference`). Excluded from the default `:med_ex` SDK\nprojection until a concrete adapter proves clean-consumer compatibility.","ref":"MedAdapters.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"MedAdapters.Inference","doc":"Behaviour contract for advisory clinical inference adapters (e.g., Ortex/ONNX).\n\nAll inference outputs carry SaMD advisory metadata and the input window's\nmeasured continuity so degraded or unverified windows are never surfaced clinically.","ref":"MedAdapters.Inference.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedAdapters.Inference.advisory_result/0","doc":"","ref":"MedAdapters.Inference.html#t:advisory_result/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedAdapters.Inference.infer/2","doc":"","ref":"MedAdapters.Inference.html#c:infer/2"},{"type":"extras","title":"Overview","doc":"# MedAdapters\n\n`med_adapters` is an **opt-in source package** inside [MedEx](../../README.md) defining behaviour contracts for real-time signal analysis and advisory ML inference. It is intentionally excluded from the default Welded `:med_ex` SDK projection (`internal_only` in `build_support/weld.exs`) so consumers do not inherit heavy ML or sidecar dependencies unless they explicitly opt in.\n\n---","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"What This Owns (and Does Not Own) - Overview","doc":"**`med_adapters` owns:**\n- `MedAdapters.Inference` — `@behaviour` and `advisory_result` type carrying `advisory_only: true`, `model_sha256`, `signal_quality_score`, and `continuity` unified directly onto `MedCore.Session.continuity_state()` (`:observed_continuous | :observed_gap | :unknown`).\n- Future opt-in adapters for in-BEAM ONNX inference (`Ortex`/`Nx`), supervised Python biosignal Ports (`NeuroKit2`, `wfdb-python`), or external media planes (`LiveKit`, `Pipecat`).\n\n**`med_adapters` does not own:**\n- Clinical persistence, outbox retries, or HL7 FHIR / DICOM delivery (those live in `med_fabric`'s `mf_store` and `mf_interop`).\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#what-this-owns-and-does-not-own"},{"type":"extras","title":"Walkthrough - Overview","doc":"```elixir\n@behaviour MedAdapters.Inference\n\n# Every inference output carries explicit advisory provenance and recording continuity:\n%{\n  advisory_only: true,\n  model_sha256: \"sha256_of_onnx_weights\",\n  signal_quality_score: 0.94,\n  continuity: :observed_continuous,\n  findings: %{murmur_probability: 0.12}\n}\n```\n\nSee `lib/med_adapters/inference.ex` and `test/med_adapters_test.exs`.\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#walkthrough"},{"type":"extras","title":"Commands & Verification - Overview","doc":"```bash\ncd core/med_adapters\nmix test\nmix credo --strict\nmix dialyzer --force-check\n```","ref":"readme.html#commands-verification"},{"type":"extras","title":"Candidate Upstream Ecosystem (Opt-In Future Adapters) - Overview","doc":"- Nx: https://github.com/elixir-nx/nx\n- Ortex: https://github.com/elixir-nx/ortex\n- Open-Stethoscope: https://github.com/NoahIsARider/open-stethoscope\n- Silero VAD: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad\n- NeuroKit2: https://github.com/neuropsychology/NeuroKit\n- WFDB-Python: https://github.com/MIT-LCP/wfdb-python\n- LiveKit: https://github.com/livekit/livekit\n- Pipecat: https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat","ref":"readme.html#candidate-upstream-ecosystem-opt-in-future-adapters"},{"type":"extras","title":"Related Packages - Overview","doc":"- [MedEx Workspace](../../README.md)\n- [MedCore](../med_core/README.md)\n- [MedRTC](../med_rtc/README.md)\n- [MedWeb](../med_web/README.md)\n- [MedPulse](../../apps/med_pulse/README.md)","ref":"readme.html#related-packages"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog\n\n## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-22","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Added - Changelog","doc":"- Initialized `med_adapters` clinical OSS adapter behaviour package skeleton and architecture specification.","ref":"changelog.html#added"},{"type":"extras","title":"License","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 nshkrdotcom\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.5"}}